    "id": "superexam-pathology-0021",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 21,
    "stem": "A 4-year-old boy presents with recurrent joint\npain involving the knees and hips. He had\nalways bruised easily, and recently the parents\nhad seen blood in his urine. A presumptive\ndiagnosis of classic hemophilia (hemophilia A)\nis made, and coagulation blood tests are\nperformed. Which of the following is the most\nlikely set of findings of coagulation screening\ntests?",
