    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "contraction of endothelial cells resulting in increased\nendothelial spaces is the most common mechanism of\nvascular leakage and is elicited by histamine,\nbradykinin, leukotrienes, substance P, etc. It is called\nthe immediate transient response because it occurs\nrapidly after exposure to the mediator. (Robbins 8th\nedition p. 47)",
