    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "dense deposit disease (MPGN type II) - is a primary\ntype MPGN associated with activation of the\nalternative pathway. This is based on the diminished\nserum levels of factor B and properdin along with\nnormal C1 an C4 levels. Ultrastructurally, type II\nMPGN is characterized by deposition of dense material\nalong the GBM proper. Natural history of patients with\nthis disease showed refractory to combined pulse\ncyclophosphamide and steroids. there is also high\nincidence of recurrence among transplant patient\ncompared to type I MPGN . Robbins 8th ed pp 928-\n929",
