    "id": "superexam-pathology-0582",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 582,
    "stem": "A 30-year-old woman presents with malaise\nand increasing fatigue. On physical\nexamination, she has anicteric sclerae and\njaundice, and laboratory evaluation finds\nelevated AST and ALT. Liver biopsy showed\nshrunken hepatocytes with highly eosinophilc\ncytoplasm and fragmented nuclei. There were\nno noted inflammatory infiltrates. Which of the\nfollowing terms best describes this process\noccurring in the hepatocytes?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Apoptosis"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Autophagy"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Heterophagy"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Necrosis"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Pinocytosis"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Apoptosis involves single cells, not large groups of\ncells, and with apoptosis the cells shrink and there is\nincreased eosinophilia of cytoplasm. The shrunken\napoptotic cells form apoptotic bodies, which may be\nengulfed by adjacent cells or macrophages. With\napoptosis there is no inflammatory response, the cell\nmembranes do not rupture, and there is no release of\nmacromolecules",
