    "explanation": "Classically the onset of bacterial pneumonia is sudden,\nwith malaise, shaking chills, fever, peripheral\nleukocytosis, and a cough with sputum production.\nBacterial infections generally result in a\npolymorphonuclear (neutrophil) response. Bacterial\ninfection of the lung (pneumonia) results in\nconsolidation of the lung, which may be patchy or\ndiffuse. Patchy consolidation of the lung is seen in\nbronchopneumonia (lobular pneumonia), while\ndiffuse involvement of an entire lobe is seen in lobar\npneumonia.",
