    "stem": "A 54-year-old female consults due to epigastric\npain. History revealed she was taking\nmefenamic acid for joint pains. Gastroscopy\nrevealed multiple, hemorrhagic ulcers <1 cm in\ndiameter scattered throughout the stomach.\nMucosal folds were normal. Biopsy of the\nlesions reveal sharply demarcated ulcers with\nnormal adjacent mucosa. Mucosal erosions\nshowed edema and hemorrhage. Which of the\nfollowing is the most likely diagnosis?",
