    "explanation": "MM is characterized by a proliferation of malignant\nplasma cells and a subsequent overabundance of\nmonoclonal paraprotein (M protein). The\nproliferation of plasma cells in MM may interfere with\nthe normal production of blood cells, resulting in\nleukopenia, anemia, and thrombocytopenia. The\naberrant antibodies that are produced lead to\nimpaired humoral immunity, and patients have a high\nprevalence of infection, especially with encapsulated\norganisms. The overproduction of these antibodies\nmay lead to hyperviscosity, amyloidosis, and renal\nfailure",
