    "explanation": "Familial hypercholesterolemia is a \"receptor disease\"\nthat is the consequence of a mutation in the gene\nencoding the receptor for low density lipoprotein\n(LDL), which is involved in the\ntransport and metabolism of cholesterol. As a\nconsequence of receptor abnormalities, there is a loss\nof feedback control and elevated levels of cholesterol\nthat induce premature\natherosclerosis, leading to a greatly increased risk of\nmyocardial infarction.",
